{
  "title": { "en": "Corners" },
  "tray": "geometry",
  "after": {
    "en": "Harris corner detection combines gradients and their correlation in a neighbourhood to distinguish corners, straight edges and flat areas. The threshold selects strong responses; next we locate a point within each response region."
  },
  "intro": [
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "To stitch overlapping photographs, we need corresponding positions in both images. Points in flat areas or along straight edges are easily confused with nearby positions; corners change in several directions and are often easier to find again."
      }
    },
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "First use Sobel and a 3×3 average to observe local change. Straight edges also change strongly, so distinguishing corners requires considering how the two directions change together."
      }
    },
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "The Harris method measures these changes with three local statistics and calculates a response. Continue the circuit through each step, then use a threshold to mark corners."
      }
    }
  ],
  "unlocks": ["harris"],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "6-1-energy",
      "kind": "graph",
      "inputs": ["in"],
      "outputs": ["out"],
      "scene": "filter",
      "tests": [
        { "label": { "en": "One corner" }, "in": "corner" },
        { "label": { "en": "Square" }, "in": { "square": { "x0": 4, "y0": 4, "s": 8 } } },
        { "label": { "en": "Straight edge" }, "in": { "stepX": { "edge": 8 } } },
        { "label": { "en": "Letter L" }, "in": { "glyph": { "letter": "L" } } }
      ],
      "hidden": [
        {
          "label": { "en": "Letter T" },
          "in": { "glyph": { "letter": "T", "lo": 0.1, "hi": 0.9, "ox": 4, "oy": 3 } }
        },
        { "label": { "en": "Shifted small square" }, "in": { "square": { "x0": 8, "y0": 2, "s": 5 } } },
        { "label": { "en": "A horizontal edge" }, "in": { "stepY": { "edge": 9 } } }
      ],
      "views": { "in": "pixels", "out": "terrain", "mid": "terrain" },
      "check": { "tolerance": 0.02 },
      "step": { "en": "Observe local change" },
      "brief": {
        "en": "Calculate horizontal and vertical gradients, square each, average each over 3×3, and add them. Compare the results at straight edges and corners."
      },
      "hint": {
        "en": "Use Sobel x and Sobel y for Gx and Gy. Multiply each image by itself, take a 3×3 average, then add the two results."
      },
      "after": {
        "en": "Local change can be strong at both edges and corners, so it cannot distinguish them alone. Next, the Harris response accounts for the relationship between the two directions."
      },
      "setup": { "target": "gradientEnergy" },
      "solution": [
        "x = sobelx(in)",
        "y = sobely(in)",
        "xx = arith[op=mul](x, x)",
        "yy = arith[op=mul](y, y)",
        "a = box3(xx)",
        "b = box3(yy)",
        "sum = arith[op=add](a, b)",
        "out <- sum"
      ],
      "naive": [
        "out <- in"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "6-1-response",
      "kind": "graph",
      "inputs": ["in"],
      "outputs": ["out"],
      "scene": "filter",
      "tests": [
        { "label": { "en": "One corner" }, "in": "corner" },
        { "label": { "en": "Square" }, "in": { "square": { "x0": 4, "y0": 4, "s": 8 } } },
        { "label": { "en": "Straight edge" }, "in": { "stepX": { "edge": 8 } } },
        { "label": { "en": "Letter L" }, "in": { "glyph": { "letter": "L" } } }
      ],
      "hidden": [
        {
          "label": { "en": "Letter T" },
          "in": { "glyph": { "letter": "T", "lo": 0.1, "hi": 0.9, "ox": 4, "oy": 3 } }
        },
        { "label": { "en": "Shifted small square" }, "in": { "square": { "x0": 8, "y0": 2, "s": 5 } } },
        { "label": { "en": "A horizontal edge" }, "in": { "stepY": { "edge": 9 } } }
      ],
      "views": { "in": "pixels", "out": "terrain", "mid": "terrain" },
      "check": { "tolerance": 0.02 },
      "step": { "en": "Distinguish edges and corners" },
      "carries": true,
      "brief": {
        "en": "Continue the circuit to calculate the Harris response. A and B are the 3×3 averages of Gx² and Gy²; C is the 3×3 average of Gx·Gy. C measures how the directions vary together: a diagonal edge can make A and B large, but C² offsets that case. Output 100 × [AB − C² − 0.05(A + B)²], and compare edges and corners."
      },
      "hint": {
        "en": "The previous circuit already has A, B and A+B. Multiply Gx and Gy and average over 3×3 for C; calculate AB−C² and 0.05×(A+B)², subtract, then multiply by 100. The 0.05 controls the penalty for edges; 100 only scales the response."
      },
      "after": {
        "en": "The Harris response combines change in both directions and their correlation: corners tend to have a strong positive response, straight edges a negative one, and flat areas a response near zero. Finally use a threshold to mark corners."
      },
      "setup": { "target": "cornerResponse" },
      "solution": [
        "ktN = const[c=0.05]()",
        "sN = const[c=100]()",
        "x = sobelx(in)",
        "y = sobely(in)",
        "xx = arith[op=mul](x, x)",
        "yy = arith[op=mul](y, y)",
        "xy = arith[op=mul](x, y)",
        "sxx = box3(xx)",
        "syy = box3(yy)",
        "sxy = box3(xy)",
        "p = arith[op=mul](sxx, syy)",
        "q = arith[op=mul](sxy, sxy)",
        "tr = arith[op=add](sxx, syy)",
        "det = arith[op=sub](p, q)",
        "tt = arith[op=mul](tr, tr)",
        "kt = arith[op=mul](tt, ktN)",
        "r = arith[op=sub](det, kt)",
        "s = arith[op=mul](r, sN)",
        "out <- s"
      ],
      "naive": [
        "x = sobelx(in)",
        "y = sobely(in)",
        "xx = arith[op=mul](x, x)",
        "yy = arith[op=mul](y, y)",
        "a = box3(xx)",
        "b = box3(yy)",
        "sum = arith[op=add](a, b)",
        "out <- sum"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "6-1",
      "step": { "en": "Mark corners" },
      "kind": "graph",
      "brief": {
        "en": "Continue the Harris response circuit: output 1 where the response exceeds 0.22 and 0 elsewhere."
      },
      "hint": {
        "en": "Connect the response to a threshold set to 0.22, then connect it to the output."
      },
      "carries": true,
      "views": { "in": "slope", "out": "pixels", "mid": "terrain" },
      "check": { "tolerance": 0.5, "mismatches": 2 },
      "scene": "filter",
      "setup": { "target": { "corners": { "threshold": 0.22 } } },
      "tests": [
        { "label": { "en": "One corner" }, "in": "corner" },
        { "label": { "en": "Square" }, "in": { "square": { "x0": 4, "y0": 4, "s": 8 } } },
        { "label": { "en": "Straight edge" }, "in": { "stepX": { "edge": 8 } } },
        { "label": { "en": "Letter L" }, "in": { "glyph": { "letter": "L" } } }
      ],
      "hidden": [
        {
          "label": { "en": "Letter T" },
          "in": { "glyph": { "letter": "T", "lo": 0.1, "hi": 0.9, "ox": 4, "oy": 3 } }
        },
        { "label": { "en": "Shifted small square" }, "in": { "square": { "x0": 8, "y0": 2, "s": 5 } } },
        { "label": { "en": "A horizontal edge" }, "in": { "stepY": { "edge": 9 } } }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "ktN = const[c=0.05]()",
        "sN = const[c=100]()",
        "x = sobelx(in)",
        "y = sobely(in)",
        "xx = arith[op=mul](x, x)",
        "yy = arith[op=mul](y, y)",
        "xy = arith[op=mul](x, y)",
        "sxx = box3(xx)",
        "syy = box3(yy)",
        "sxy = box3(xy)",
        "p = arith[op=mul](sxx, syy)",
        "q = arith[op=mul](sxy, sxy)",
        "tr = arith[op=add](sxx, syy)",
        "det = arith[op=sub](p, q)",
        "tt = arith[op=mul](tr, tr)",
        "kt = arith[op=mul](tt, ktN)",
        "r = arith[op=sub](det, kt)",
        "s = arith[op=mul](r, sN)",
        "t = threshold[t=0.22](s)",
        "out <- t"
      ],
      "naive": [
        "sN = const[c=100]()",
        "x = sobelx(in)",
        "y = sobely(in)",
        "xx = arith[op=mul](x, x)",
        "yy = arith[op=mul](y, y)",
        "a = arith[op=add](xx, yy)",
        "s = arith[op=mul](a, sN)",
        "t = threshold[t=0.22](s)",
        "out <- t"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
